metic images of operands and operators, and operators include the minus sign with no non-negativity bound. The domain therefore admits negative running values, which are beyond grade 3 Q2. The printed expression_str values are all non-negative, but they bound F07 and F03 only, not F04. F01 ('number sentence', gated by 'expression') is not in NOT_YET_KNOWN, so it is not flagged. F02 and F06 introduce and use 'order of operations' within this lc's gates, and F06's left-to-right rule is correct for addition and subtraction only. F03 prints only expression_str values that are non-negative, with 3 or 4 operands and operands of 1 or 2 digits. F05 prints the observed answers, which are non-negative. F07 is within scope. Note: declared variant context word_problem has no family that renders it differently from pure, so it adds no distinct learner text. This is not a Rule 1 or Rule 2 fault.\"}",
